{"causes": ["The initial establishment of the Servite Order in 1233 provided the foundational structure for Benizi's later leadership.", "The decrees of the Second Council of Lyon in 1274 threatened the existence of all newer mendicant orders, necessitating strong leadership for the Servites' survival.", "The widespread spiritual fervor and desire for monastic reform in 13th-century Italy created an environment ripe for the emergence of influential religious figures like Benizi."], "effects": ["Philip Benizi's leadership led to the significant revival and international expansion of the Servite Order across Europe.", "His successful advocacy at the Second Council of Lyon ensured the continued existence of the Servite Order, preventing its suppression.", "His canonization in 1671 solidified his veneration within the Catholic Church and elevated the profile of the Servite Order."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "second-council-of-lyon", "sourceName": "Second Council of Lyon", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "philip-benizi-de-damiani", "targetName": "Philip Benizi de Damiani", "context": "The Council's decrees threatening mendicant orders directly influenced Philip Benizi's efforts to secure the Servites' survival in 1274."}, {"sourceSlug": "philip-benizi-de-damiani", "sourceName": "Philip Benizi de Damiani", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "italy", "targetName": "Italy", "context": "Philip Benizi's birthplace, primary activities, and death all occurred within the geographic region of Italy during the 13th century."}, {"sourceSlug": "philip-benizi-de-damiani", "sourceName": "Philip Benizi de Damiani", "verb": "SUCCEEDS", "targetSlug": "boniface-of-florence", "targetName": "Boniface of Florence", "context": "Philip Benizi succeeded Boniface of Florence as the fifth General Superior of the Servite Order in 1267."}, {"sourceSlug": "philip-benizi-de-damiani", "sourceName": "Philip Benizi de Damiani", "verb": "TRANSFORMS", "targetSlug": "order-of-servants-of-mary",